# MOVED (DR-01).
#
# The demo scheduler is deployed through the shipped per-tenant wrapper, which
# handles the state backend safely per tenant:
#
#   ./infra/deploy.sh demo plan
#   ./infra/deploy.sh demo apply
#
# It reads these files (copy the committed .example templates, then fill in):
#   infra/tenants/demo.tfvars          (from infra/tenants/demo.tfvars.example)
#   infra/tenants/demo.backend.hcl     (from infra/tenants/demo.backend.hcl.example)
#
# Or generate infra/tenants/demo.tfvars from the landing-zone outputs:
#   demo/landing-zone/render-demo-tfvars.sh --alert-email you@example.com
#
# Do NOT run `terraform -chdir=infra/scheduler ... -var-file=../demo/...`: with
# -chdir, a relative -var-file resolves against infra/scheduler, not the repo
# root, and a bare destroy there targets whatever backend that folder was last
# initialised with. Always use deploy.sh demo (or deploy.sh with -reconfigure).
